==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈøystʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|øystʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|austr}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*austrą}}.

====Adverb====
{{is-adv|austar|austast}}

# [[east]], [[eastward]] (designating movement to the east)
# in the east (only used together with a prepositional phrase indicating a more precise location, except when used comparatively)

====Noun====
{{is-noun|n|austurs|-}}

# [[east]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s||au|st|u|r|pl=-}}

===Etymology 2===
Related to the verb {{m|is|ausa}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|austurs|austrar}}

# the act of [[draw]]ing [water] or [[ladle#Verb|ladling]]
# [[waste]], [[squandering]]

